# SCSS Conventions

## Adding styles for a new section

1. Create `src/styles/sections/_<same-base-as-section-file>.scss` (e.g. `_section-feature-grid.scss` for `section-feature-grid.liquid`).
2. Add `@forward '<partial-name-without-_and_extension>';` to `src/styles/sections/index.scss` (order only matters for cascade if selectors overlap).
3. Prefer **section root** CSS custom properties set from Liquid for merchant-controlled values.

## File organization

```
src/styles/
├── theme.scss                    # Main entry: imports base + sections
├── base/
│   ├── _variables.scss           # Design tokens ($space-xs..xl, $font-stack-system)
│   ├── _breakpoints.scss         # $breakpoints map + mq-up() mixin
│   ├── _fonts.scss               # Font-face / typography base
│   └── _section-wrapper.scss     # Shared section container styles
├── components/
│   ├── _theme-modal.scss         # Reusable modal component
│   └── _image-lightbox.scss      # Image lightbox overlay
└── sections/
    ├── index.scss                # @forward all section partials
    ├── _header.scss
    ├── _footer.scss
    ├── _main-product.scss
    ├── _main-collection.scss
    ├── _cart-drawer.scss
    └── ...
```

## Import system

- `theme.scss` uses `@use` for base, `@use 'sections/index'` for all sections
- Section files use `@forward` in `sections/index.scss`
- Vite `loadPaths: ['src/styles']` enables bare imports like `@use 'base/variables'`
- Use `@use 'base/breakpoints' as *` to get `mq-up()` without namespace

## Breakpoints (mobile-first)

```scss
@use 'base/breakpoints' as *;

.element {
  padding: 1rem;

  @include mq-up('md') {  // 48em = 768px
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  @include mq-up('lg') {  // 62em = 992px
    padding: 3rem;
  }
}
```

| Token | Value | Approx px |
|-------|-------|-----------|
| `sm`  | 36em  | 576px     |
| `md`  | 48em  | 768px     |
| `lg`  | 62em  | 992px     |
| `xl`  | 75em  | 1200px    |

## Naming convention

- Section-scoped BEM-like prefixes: `mcol__hero`, `mcol__card-img`, `pdp-gallery__thumb`
- Short prefixes per section (not full BEM block names)
- Modifier classes: `mcol__pag-arrow--disabled`, `cart-drawer--open`
- State classes: `is-ajax-loading`, `is-active`

## Design tokens

```scss
$space-xs: 0.25rem;
$space-sm: 0.5rem;
$space-md: 1rem;
$space-lg: 1.5rem;
$space-xl: 2rem;
```

- Prefer CSS custom properties for values controlled by Liquid settings
- Use Sass variables for static design tokens shared across partials

## Typography and font size (merchant scale)

**Source of truth:** `snippets/css-variables.liquid` outputs `:root` custom properties. The merchant setting **Theme settings → Typography → Base font size** (`settings.font_size_base`, typically 16 / 18 / 20 px) rescales the whole step system and the fluid `clamp()` math for larger steps.

**Use these tokens for `font-size`** (and similar) in `src/styles/**/*.scss`, in `{% stylesheet %}` blocks, and anywhere else the DOM can see `:root`:

| Variable | Typical role |
|----------|----------------|
| `--font-size-xs` | Fine print, micro labels |
| `--font-size-sm` | Secondary UI, captions |
| `--font-size-base` | Body-scale UI (fluid clamp) |
| `--font-size-lg` | Emphasis, card titles |
| `--font-size-xl` | Section subheads |
| `--font-size-2xl` | Large subheads |
| `--font-size-3xl` | Display / hero titles |
| `--font-size-4xl` | Largest display |

**Line-height tokens** (optional, pair with type): `--line-height-tight`, `--line-height-snug`, `--line-height-normal`, `--line-height-relaxed`.

**SCSS pattern:** always include a literal fallback so unstyled or partial loads still render sensibly:

```scss
.card__title {
  font-size: var(--font-size-lg, 1.25rem);
  line-height: var(--line-height-snug, 1.25);
}
```

**When to use `em` instead:** keep `font-size` in `em` when the intent is **relative to an ancestor** (e.g. nested rich text, fractional stacked prices, badges inside a parent that already uses a token). Do **not** introduce raw `rem`/`px` for user-facing type that should track the global scale—map to the closest `--font-size-*` step.

**Section- or block-specific multipliers:** if Liquid exposes a scale (e.g. `--pdp-title-scale`), wrap the token: `calc(var(--font-size-3xl, 2.625rem) * var(--pdp-title-scale, 1))`.

**Global heading/body:** `src/styles/base/_fonts.scss` and `assets/critical.css` already tie `body` and heading elements to these variables—new components should stay consistent with that hierarchy.

**Reference:** `docs/Font Size Base — Typographic Scale System.md` for ratios and design rationale.

## CSS custom properties pattern

Liquid sets properties on the section root:
```liquid
<section style="--collection-cols: {{ cols }};">
```

SCSS consumes them:
```scss
.col-grid {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--collection-cols, 4), 1fr);
}
```

## Critical vs non-critical CSS

- `assets/critical.css` — manually maintained, loaded with `preload` in `<head>`
- `assets/theme.css` — Vite output from SCSS, loaded normally
- Section-specific CSS can also use `{% stylesheet %}` in Liquid (deduplicated by Shopify)
